6.4 Integration Patterns
Request-Reply (Synchronous)
Salesforce sends request and waits for response
Flow
Request sent
External system processes
Immediate response returned
Use Case
Real-time validation (e.g., payment check)
Fire-and-Forget (Asynchronous)
Salesforce sends request and does not wait
Flow
Request sent
No response expected
Use Case
Logging systems
Notifications
Batch Integration
Processes large datasets periodically
Flow
Data collected
Sent in batches
Processed asynchronously
Use Case
Nightly data sync
Data warehousing
